---
/* An addendum, the same shape as /tests/older-names/ and for the same reason.

   That page exists because a skater arrives holding the name of a test that no
   longer exists. This one exists because they arrive holding a name for a MOVEMENT
   that the guide does not use — their coach's word, or an older one. Without a way
   in, an unfamiliar name is a dead end.

   The guide's own rule does not move: the governing body's word is the name of the
   page, and nothing here renames anything. These are ways IN.

   Generated from the collection rather than written out, so a name recorded on an
   element appears here automatically and the two cannot disagree. Short on purpose:
   nothing goes in that cannot be pointed at a source. */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Unverified from '../../components/Unverified.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url.js';

const elements = await getCollection('elements');

/* One row per alias, not per element — the reader has the alias and wants the
   page. Where a movement has eight entries the row names the movement once and
   links to the family, which is what "open chassé" means to somebody anyway. */
const byAlias = new Map();
for (const e of elements)
  for (const a of e.data.aliases ?? []) {
    if (!byAlias.has(a)) byAlias.set(a, []);
    byAlias.get(a).push(e);
  }
const rows = [...byAlias.entries()]
  .map(([alias, es]) => ({ alias, es: es.sort((x, y) => x.data.name.localeCompare(y.data.name)) }))
  .sort((x, y) => x.alias.localeCompare(y.alias));
---
<Base title="Other names" subtitle="Names skaters and coaches use for movements this guide files under something else.">
  <h1>Other names</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Your coach's word for something and the governing body's word are not always the same.
    This guide files a movement under British Ice Skating's name; here are the other names
    it goes by, so a name you already know is a way in rather than a dead end.
  </p>

  <Unverified />

  {rows.length === 0
    ? <p>No alternative names are recorded yet.</p>
    : <ul class="aliases">
        {rows.map(r =>
          <li>
            <b>{r.alias}</b>
            <span>
              {r.es.length > 4
                ? <>{r.es.length} elements — <a href={url(`elements/${r.es[0].id}/`)}>{r.es[0].data.name}</a> and the rest of the family</>
                : r.es.map((e, i) => <>{i > 0 ? ', ' : ''}<a href={url(`elements/${e.id}/`)}>{e.data.name}</a></>)}
            </span>
          </li>)}
      </ul>}

  <h2>What is not here</h2>
  <p>
    A name only goes on this list once it can be pointed at a source — a governing body's
    own document, or a dictionary. Names that are certainly in use but that nobody has
    checked are left off rather than guessed at, which is the same rule the rest of the
    guide runs on. If a name you use is missing, that is worth telling us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Older <em>test</em> names are a separate question and are on
    <a href={url('tests/older-names/')}>older test names</a>. If you are looking for a
    movement and do not know any of its names, <a href={url('search/')}>search</a> also
    matches edge codes and descriptions.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .aliases{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 1rem}
  .aliases li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.1rem;
    padding:.7rem 0;min-height:44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}
  .aliases b{font-family:ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;font-weight:600}
  .aliases span{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.45}
</style>
